= The Democratic Party Challenges Erim

As the motion of interpellation comes to parliament, the votes of Ecevit’s supporters in CHP, MGP and many AP members join those of the DP to pass the motion. What was expected to be another unsuccessful attempt to challenge Erim's government has instead turned into a humiliating parliamentary defeat, shocking the entire political establishment in Ankara, for even many deputies from the AP,  who had so far endorsed the military's attempts eroding the 1961 constitution, have went against their party leader. With his effectively non-existent authority so blatantly refused in parliament, Erim sees no reason to even entertain the idea of another day as a PM and issues his resignation.

However, our unexpected parliamentary victory has come at a considerable political cost. Upon finding out Ecevit has formed an informal alliance with 3 other parties without informing the General Chairman, İnönü essentially raged in disbelief. Ecevit's actions has directly undermined the party leadership's efforts to maintain stability and keeping parliament intact as it considerably angered the Army. İnönü is increasingly starting to see Ecevit as a reckless, irresponsible delinquent that dares to act on the behalf of existing CHP leadership. The tensions between the 2 man at this point was neither ideological nor political, but directly revolved around İnönü's frustration at Ecevit's unruly and disrespectful behavior.

